1
00:00:03,630 --> 00:00:06,210
And here's another interesting weather fact.

2
00:00:06,260 --> 00:00:08,370
Another? Great!

3
00:00:09,090 --> 00:00:12,340
Changes in jet streams can affect the speed

4
00:00:12,340 --> 00:00:14,650
at which the Earth rotates on its axis,

5
00:00:14,650 --> 00:00:18,470
so bad weather can actually make the day longer.

6
00:00:18,470 --> 00:00:21,680
Well, there must be a hell of a storm somewhere.

7
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:24,830
Joke if you must,

8
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:26,930
but you're going to miss these moments.

9
00:00:26,930 --> 00:00:28,720
With Leonard home in a few days,

10
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:31,710
this was your last time driving me to the grocery store.

11
00:00:31,710 --> 00:00:33,930
You know, I will miss this.

12
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:36,920
I'll tell you what, if my apples are mealy,

13
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:40,850
we'll hit the produce section for one last crazy blowout.

14
00:00:41,690 --> 00:00:43,960
Heck, you can even push the cart.

15
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:48,190
Please don't take my looking forward to Leonard's return

16
00:00:48,190 --> 00:00:51,850
as criticism of the job you've been doing in his absence.

17
00:00:51,850 --> 00:00:53,520
I won't.

18
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:57,150
That criticism will come later in your report card.

19
00:00:57,150 --> 00:00:59,570
Yeah, I didn't stay for the detention,

20
00:00:59,570 --> 00:01:01,660
I'm not gonna read the report card.

21
00:01:05,240 --> 00:01:05,900
Hello.

22
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:07,550
Leonard!

23
00:01:07,550 --> 00:01:08,400
- Shh, shh. - Hi!

24
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:09,840
- Keep your voice down. - Oh, my God.

25
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:11,270
You weren't supposed to be here till Sunday!

26
00:01:11,270 --> 00:01:12,420
We finished the experiment early,

27
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:14,150
so I thought I'd come home and surprise you.

28
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:15,600
Oh, my gosh, why are we whispering?

29
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:16,700
I didn't tell Sheldon,

30
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,260
so we could have a few days alone.

31
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:20,360
Oh, that is so romantic.

32
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:22,820
Uh, sure, that's why I did it.

33
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:26,470
Oh... I just cannot believe you're here.

34
00:01:26,470 --> 00:01:28,160
Penny, it's your lucky day!

35
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:30,850
Three of the eggs are clearly not jumbo.

36
00:01:30,850 --> 00:01:32,740
Grab your keys.

37
00:01:59,230 --> 00:02:01,080
Uh, Stuart, I was wondering

38
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:03,550
- if you could help me find something. - Happy to,

39
00:02:03,550 --> 00:02:06,130
unless it's hope or a reason to live.

40
00:02:07,050 --> 00:02:10,210
Oh, you make me laugh, sad clown.

41
00:02:12,010 --> 00:02:12,960
Anyhoo...

42
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:15,210
Leonard will be back in a couple days

43
00:02:15,210 --> 00:02:17,590
and I need a welcome-home gift for him.

44
00:02:17,590 --> 00:02:20,040
As he's been at sea, perhaps something

45
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:23,110
with a nautical theme might be appropriate.

46
00:02:23,110 --> 00:02:25,420
Okay, well, I don't know how much you want to spend,

47
00:02:25,420 --> 00:02:29,230
but I do have this pretty cool Aquaman statue.

48
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:34,260
Aquaman?

49
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:37,480
Oh, this isn't a gag gift, Stuart.

50
00:02:38,390 --> 00:02:39,220
Yeah, just as well.

51
00:02:39,220 --> 00:02:41,210
It's a pretty rare piece.

52
00:02:41,210 --> 00:02:43,850
I'd rather just sell it to a real collector.

53
00:02:43,850 --> 00:02:46,780
I'm a real collector.

54
00:02:46,780 --> 00:02:48,830
How rare is it?

55
00:02:48,830 --> 00:02:50,450
Oh, I shouldn't even have mentioned it.

56
00:02:50,450 --> 00:02:52,740
How about a Batman squirt gun?

57
00:02:53,490 --> 00:02:55,060
Don't try and trick me

58
00:02:55,060 --> 00:02:56,830
into buying something I don't want.

59
00:02:56,830 --> 00:02:59,080
Now let's talk Aquaman.

60
00:03:00,190 --> 00:03:03,120
What were they thinking, putting Doctor Octopus's mind

61
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:05,190
in Spider-Man's body?

62
00:03:05,190 --> 00:03:07,120
Well, I've been quite enjoying that.

63
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:09,440
It combines all the superhero fun of Spider-Man

64
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:12,660
with all the body-switching shenanigans of Freaky Friday.

65
00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:16,400
"Both versions: original and Lohan."

66
00:03:16,910 --> 00:03:18,800
"Both versions: original and Lohan."

67
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:19,620
You're an idiot.

68
00:03:20,350 --> 00:03:22,090
Hey, what's your problem?

69
00:03:22,090 --> 00:03:24,100
I'm sorry, I've been kind of snippy lately.

70
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:26,580
It's probably this stupid diet I'm on.

71
00:03:26,580 --> 00:03:27,860
Why are you on a diet?

72
00:03:27,860 --> 00:03:29,860
I've put on a couple pounds.

73
00:03:31,070 --> 00:03:33,440
Had to buy these pants in the men's section.

74
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:38,100
Well, we've all seen your mom.

75
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:40,250
That Butterball turkey

76
00:03:40,250 --> 00:03:42,600
was bound to come home to roost.

77
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:47,790
$1,200! That's my final offer!

78
00:03:47,790 --> 00:03:49,950
All right, Sheldon, you win.

79
00:03:49,950 --> 00:03:51,840
I'm sure Leonard is gonna love this.

80
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:54,940
Oh, right, a present for Leonard.

81
00:03:55,810 --> 00:03:58,140
You better throw in that squirt gun.

82
00:03:58,930 --> 00:03:59,720
Yeah, I don't know.

83
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:03,180
This squirt gun, it's, uh, it's pretty rare.

84
00:04:07,750 --> 00:04:11,470
And this is me doing the Titanic pose on the boat.

85
00:04:13,230 --> 00:04:13,840
And... oh.

86
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:16,350
That's me getting rescued after I fell in.

87
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,740
- Oh, that's the pizza. - Yep.

88
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:22,760
- Here's some money. - Thank you.

89
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:24,430
And I'm gonna hit the head.

90
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:26,900
That's what us salty sea dogs say

91
00:04:26,900 --> 00:04:28,700
when we have to go pee-pee.

92
00:04:30,830 --> 00:04:31,860
$22.50.

93
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:33,800
Okay, here's, uh, $25. Keep the change.

94
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:34,620
Seriously?

95
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:37,860
I just walked up, like, four flights of stairs.

96
00:04:38,490 --> 00:04:39,920
Okay.

97
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:41,640
Well, here's, um...

98
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:43,620
30-something cents

99
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:45,940
and a promise I won't call your boss

100
00:04:45,940 --> 00:04:48,640
and tell him you reek of marijuana.

101
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:52,930
Oh, Penny, I see you've ordered pizza.

102
00:04:52,930 --> 00:04:54,310
I have Chinese food.

103
00:04:54,310 --> 00:04:55,440
That's nice.

104
00:04:55,440 --> 00:04:58,960
Oh, that's a rather earthy cologne.

105
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:03,650
My uncle used to wear that.

106
00:05:04,390 --> 00:05:06,270
Perhaps we can enjoy one last meal together

107
00:05:06,270 --> 00:05:08,440
- before Leonard returns. - Yeah, thanks,

108
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:10,070
but I kind of feel like eating alone tonight, so...

109
00:05:10,070 --> 00:05:11,060
Are you sure?

110
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:13,790
With your Italian pizza and my Chinese noodles,

111
00:05:13,790 --> 00:05:15,900
we could play Marco Polo.

112
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:18,460
I mean, of course, a reenactment of a meal

113
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:21,010
in the life of Marco Polo the Venetian explorer,

114
00:05:21,010 --> 00:05:24,580
not Marco Polo the terrifying water sport.

115
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:27,820
Uh, yeah, it sounds fun, but no thanks.

116
00:05:28,110 --> 00:05:29,100
Have a good night!

117
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:30,870
What, now... do you have company?

118
00:05:30,870 --> 00:05:32,300
No. No, no, no.

119
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:34,000
You know what? Th-The toilet's been doing that.

120
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,220
I called the building manager, so...

121
00:05:35,220 --> 00:05:36,730
Oh, I can take a look at it.

122
00:05:36,730 --> 00:05:39,050
I'm quite familiar with plumbing.

123
00:05:39,050 --> 00:05:40,420
Not to brag,

124
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:44,170
but I spent most of fifth grade with my head in a toilet.

125
00:05:44,170 --> 00:05:44,780
Yeah, no, no, no.

126
00:05:44,780 --> 00:05:46,460
You know what, Sheldon, it's okay.

127
00:05:46,460 --> 00:05:48,150
You don't have to go into the bathroom.

128
00:05:48,150 --> 00:05:49,750
That's curious.

129
00:05:49,750 --> 00:05:51,340
If there's no one here,

130
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:54,630
why are there two glasses of wine on the table?

131
00:05:54,630 --> 00:05:55,870
Oh.

132
00:05:55,870 --> 00:05:57,770
Well, you know, I-I've got two hands

133
00:05:57,770 --> 00:05:59,870
and a bit of a drinking problem.

134
00:06:01,250 --> 00:06:01,750
Of course.

135
00:06:01,750 --> 00:06:02,770
Ask a silly question.

136
00:06:05,170 --> 00:06:06,230
That's odd.

137
00:06:06,230 --> 00:06:07,100
Um, what?

138
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:10,090
There are takeout containers in the trash can.

139
00:06:10,090 --> 00:06:12,310
So? That's my dinner from last night.

140
00:06:12,310 --> 00:06:15,560
What's odd is they're in the trash can.

141
00:06:15,910 --> 00:06:16,410
Okay.

142
00:06:16,410 --> 00:06:17,840
Look, honey, I promise there's no one's here.

143
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:18,720
I've had a long day.

144
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:20,980
I just want to have a quiet dinner by myself.

145
00:06:20,980 --> 00:06:22,910
Oh, very well.

146
00:06:22,910 --> 00:06:26,020
I'm no stranger to enjoying the pleasures of solitude.

147
00:06:27,190 --> 00:06:28,980
- Oh! - What?

148
00:06:29,870 --> 00:06:31,730
Have you gotten Leonard a welcome-home gift yet?

149
00:06:31,730 --> 00:06:32,840
- No. - Oh, great.

150
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:36,140
Do you want to go halfsies on a $200 squirt gun?

151
00:06:39,470 --> 00:06:40,400
Hi, honey.

152
00:06:41,380 --> 00:06:43,810
I made some brownies. You want one?

153
00:06:43,810 --> 00:06:46,510
You're kidding, right?

154
00:06:46,510 --> 00:06:47,570
I mean, you know

155
00:06:47,570 --> 00:06:49,580
I'm trying to lose weight.

156
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:53,080
God, I thought we were partners in this marriage.

157
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:54,850
We are. Stop it.

158
00:06:54,850 --> 00:06:56,720
And for the last time, you're not fat.

159
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:58,700
Really? Tell that to the bathroom scale,

160
00:06:58,700 --> 00:07:00,790
'cause one of you is lying.

161
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:04,050
Fine, forget I asked.

162
00:07:04,050 --> 00:07:05,630
How was dinner at your mom's?

163
00:07:05,630 --> 00:07:06,430
Awful.

164
00:07:06,430 --> 00:07:09,300
I had to rub her ointment all over her again.

165
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:10,690
Why can't she do it?

166
00:07:10,690 --> 00:07:14,170
'Cause we've got a deeply unhealthy relationship.

167
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:16,550
Which reminds me,

168
00:07:16,550 --> 00:07:18,910
do you think you can get any samples of this from work?

169
00:07:18,910 --> 00:07:20,340
This was supposed to last her a month,

170
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:21,410
but they didn't take into account

171
00:07:21,410 --> 00:07:23,670
the square footage of her back.

172
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,760
Let me see.

173
00:07:28,200 --> 00:07:30,180
How long have you been putting this on her?

174
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:30,940
I don't know.

175
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:32,460
Few weeks. Why?

176
00:07:32,460 --> 00:07:34,720
This is really strong estrogen cream.

177
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:36,640
Please tell me you've been wearing gloves.

178
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:39,490
Like these swollen sausages could fit in gloves.

179
00:07:41,060 --> 00:07:43,720
Howie, the estrogen's getting absorbed by your skin.

180
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:44,690
That's why you've been

181
00:07:44,690 --> 00:07:49,430
all bloated and moody and a giant pain in the ass.

182
00:07:49,430 --> 00:07:51,860
You're full of estrogen and you don't act like that.

183
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:53,060
That's 'cause I'm a woman.

184
00:07:53,060 --> 00:07:56,380
I've had years of practice riding the dragon.

185
00:07:58,440 --> 00:07:59,050
Fine.

186
00:07:59,050 --> 00:08:01,280
I'll wear gloves next time.

187
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:02,460
It's still gonna take a few weeks

188
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:04,790
for the hormones to leave your system.

189
00:08:04,790 --> 00:08:06,530
I feel so stupid.

190
00:08:06,530 --> 00:08:08,300
And fat.

191
00:08:09,390 --> 00:08:10,510
It's okay.

192
00:08:10,510 --> 00:08:12,500
You still look great to me.

193
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:14,470
In fact, why don't we go in the bedroom

194
00:08:14,470 --> 00:08:16,270
and I'll prove it to you?

195
00:08:16,860 --> 00:08:17,920
Sex? Really?

196
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:20,610
I mean, that's just your solution to everything!

197
00:08:23,150 --> 00:08:25,050
Oh, and here's a fun thing.

198
00:08:25,050 --> 00:08:26,220
I worked it out so that there are

199
00:08:26,220 --> 00:08:28,270
two different words for spoon:

200
00:08:28,270 --> 00:08:30,670
"Planko" and "Janko."

201
00:08:30,670 --> 00:08:32,770
"Planko" is a spoon with food,

202
00:08:32,770 --> 00:08:35,500
"Janko" is a spoon without food.

203
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:39,390
"Janko" is spelled with a silent "Ptang."

204
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:43,320
Sheldon, you're not even listening

205
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:45,490
to the rules of my made-up language.

206
00:08:45,490 --> 00:08:46,690
Yes, I am.

207
00:08:46,690 --> 00:08:48,680
Then what does "tweepadock" mean?

208
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:52,240
Elephant?

209
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,970
Lucky guess.

210
00:08:56,450 --> 00:08:57,390
I'm sorry.

211
00:08:57,390 --> 00:09:00,960
I'm just distracted by something that happened over at Penny's.

212
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:02,120
What happened?

213
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:05,030
I fear Penny is being unfaithful to Leonard.

214
00:09:05,030 --> 00:09:06,060
What?

215
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:07,800
She claimed to be alone

216
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:10,980
when there was obviously someone else in her apartment.

217
00:09:10,980 --> 00:09:13,620
I have no choice but to assume the worst,

218
00:09:13,620 --> 00:09:15,690
given Leonard's lengthy sea voyage

219
00:09:15,690 --> 00:09:19,190
and her famously ravenous nether regions.

220
00:09:20,260 --> 00:09:22,080
I don't think Penny would cheat on Leonard.

221
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:23,710
Oh, really?

222
00:09:26,020 --> 00:09:29,310
She and I once had a staring contest.

223
00:09:29,310 --> 00:09:33,140
She clapped really loud and made me blink.

224
00:09:33,140 --> 00:09:37,020
It's a small leap from there to sexual infidelity.

225
00:09:38,410 --> 00:09:40,160
You're being ridiculous.

226
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:43,020
Amy, there were Chinese food containers...

227
00:09:43,020 --> 00:09:45,840
in the trash can.

228
00:09:47,100 --> 00:09:48,900
Poor Leonard.

229
00:09:54,350 --> 00:09:55,540
Do you hear anything?

230
00:09:55,540 --> 00:09:57,980
I hear a woman's voice.

231
00:09:57,980 --> 00:09:58,940
Is it Penny?

232
00:09:58,940 --> 00:10:00,690
No, it's you.

233
00:10:03,130 --> 00:10:05,980
All right, I hear whispering and giggling.

234
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:07,560
Now I think I hear kissing.

235
00:10:07,560 --> 00:10:10,230
Yeah, like you know what kissing sounds like.

236
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:13,770
There's kissing in Star Trek, smarty-pants.

237
00:10:14,290 --> 00:10:15,670
Let me listen.

238
00:10:18,260 --> 00:10:19,820
Sounds like Leonard.

239
00:10:19,820 --> 00:10:20,890
Please.

240
00:10:20,890 --> 00:10:23,140
Why would Leonard come home early

241
00:10:23,140 --> 00:10:24,950
and waste his time kissing Penny

242
00:10:24,950 --> 00:10:27,740
when he could be hanging out with his best buddy?

243
00:10:29,530 --> 00:10:30,950
Yeah, that's it.

244
00:10:30,950 --> 00:10:32,380
I'm catching her in the act.

245
00:10:32,380 --> 00:10:34,370
No, Sheldon, don't.

246
00:10:35,030 --> 00:10:35,950
Aha!

247
00:10:35,950 --> 00:10:37,420
What the hell?!

248
00:10:37,420 --> 00:10:38,190
Leonard?

249
00:10:38,190 --> 00:10:40,560
Sheldon, you cannot just barge in here like that!

250
00:10:40,570 --> 00:10:42,150
Right.

251
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:46,520
Penny!

252
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:50,130
Penny! Penny!

253
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:53,620
Are you going to answer the door

254
00:10:53,620 --> 00:10:56,440
or should I open it and say "Aha" again?

255
00:11:00,830 --> 00:11:01,970
I'm sorry, Sheldon.

256
00:11:01,970 --> 00:11:03,040
I should've told you I was back.

257
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:05,070
I just wanted to have a couple days alone with Penny.

258
00:11:05,070 --> 00:11:07,230
Oh, no, I should apologize.

259
00:11:07,230 --> 00:11:09,080
Uh, I never realized to what extent

260
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:11,220
our friendship was a burden to you.

261
00:11:11,220 --> 00:11:12,940
That is not fair.

262
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:16,340
I complain about what a burden it is at least once a month.

263
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:18,060
Oh, no, no, let's not sugarcoat this.

264
00:11:18,060 --> 00:11:21,770
You find me finicky, pedantic and annoying.

265
00:11:21,770 --> 00:11:23,180
No, he doesn't.

266
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:26,780
I actually have used those exact words before.

267
00:11:27,910 --> 00:11:29,380
In that order.

268
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:32,280
Well, Leonard, I think it's high time

269
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:35,610
you and I address the "Tweepadock" in the room.

270
00:11:37,060 --> 00:11:38,350
- The what? - Amy?

271
